// 2026-11-18 (issue #7, Phase 2/3): multi-statement guard body with local lets.
//
// Phase 2 coverage-matrix finding: `outlinable_stmt` returns true for a
// `Let` whose expr is outlinable, so a body like
//   when a >= 10 { let u = -a; let c = a as Int; endprogram Print#(u + c); };
// passes the outline gate. But the cold-function emission (reassigned_lets
// cleared, let_bindings reset, no body-local-let registration) DROPS the let
// bindings — the IR computed `(-a) + a` instead of `u + c`, and `c` silently
// became 0. The Phase 1 post-outline validation caught this live:
//   "error: cold function `@txn_n_cold_0` references `c` which has no storage
//    in this module … the value would silently become 0."
//
// Phase 3 repair: the outline gate now requires body.len() == 1. Multi-
// statement guard bodies stay inline (correct — they read %state directly
// via the normal emission path). This fixture documents the hole: it builds
// with NO validation diagnostic, the guard is NOT outlined (no _cold_
// function), and the program prints the correct value (0 = -10 + 10).
let a: Int = 3;
let b: Int = 4;

node n [a < 10][a >= 10] {
  a = a + 1;
  when a >= 10 {
    let u: Int = -a;
    let c: Int = a as Int;
    endprogram Print#(u + c);
  };
};
